COSMIC for Debian 13 "trixie"
=============================

An unofficial build of the COSMIC desktop (pop-os/cosmic-epoch tag
epoch-1.11.0) for Debian 13. Most of it works as on Pop!_OS. The things below
work differently on Debian; all were found by the package's tests in a
virtual machine.


Login screen
------------

The COSMIC login screen (cosmic-greeter) is installed but not enabled; the
session can be chosen as "COSMIC" in another display manager. To use the
COSMIC login screen instead, install greetd and run:

    sudo ln -sf /usr/lib/systemd/system/cosmic-greeter.service \
        /etc/systemd/system/display-manager.service

It types with the system's keyboard layout, the one in /etc/default/keyboard.
Change it with "sudo dpkg-reconfigure keyboard-configuration"; the login
screen uses it the next time it starts. (The layout a user picks in Settings
applies in their session and on their lock screen, not on the login screen.)
Each time the login screen starts, the package writes this layout to
/var/lib/cosmic-greeter/.config/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicComp/v1/xkb_config
(pop-os/cosmic-greeter#519: the login screen itself no longer does). Once
that file is edited by hand, it is left alone.


Language
--------

Choosing a language in Settings (Region & language) changes nothing: Debian's
systemd-localed does not let programs change the system language, and the
login screen does not use the per-user language. Set the language for the
whole system instead:

    sudo dpkg-reconfigure locales

Generate the locale, choose it as the default (this writes
/etc/default/locale), then log out and in again. Settings' "Add language"
lists only the locales generated this way.


Password, users, computer name
------------------------------

Settings' Change password, Add user and the device name (About) do nothing
on Debian, without an error: Settings asks AccountsService and hostnamed
without letting them ask for a password, and Debian's polkit requires one.
Use a terminal instead:

    passwd
    sudo adduser NAME
    sudo hostnamectl hostname NAME


Printing
--------

Printing needs CUPS, which the package recommends (cups). Without it Print
Settings says "Printing service not available".


Keyring
-------

With libpam-gnome-keyring (recommended) the login password unlocks the
keyring. On a new user's very first login the new login keyring may not store
passwords until the next login; log out and in once.


Messages in the journal
-----------------------

cosmic-session logs "Failed to sync xkb_config with systemd-localed" whenever
the keyboard layout changes: it tries to copy the layout to the system
settings, which Debian's systemd-localed refuses. The session's layout is not
affected.


More
----

The VM tests and the list of what they check, with every issue found, are in
tests/trixie (ACCEPTANCE.md) of the source repository,
